## Risks

| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation |
|------|------------|------------|
| psutil API differences across Python versions | Low | Pin psutil version, test on Python 3.8+ |
| systemd not available (non-systemd distros) | Low | PRD targets Ubuntu 24.04 only |
| Install.sh runs as root, potential security | Medium | Validate inputs, create dedicated user, minimal permissions |
| Network partition causes metric loss | Low | Retry with backoff up to 5min; after that, skip (acceptable per PRD) |

## Rollback Plan

1. `sudo systemctl stop serverpulse-agent && sudo systemctl disable serverpulse-agent`
2. `sudo rm /etc/systemd/system/serverpulse-agent.service && sudo systemctl daemon-reload`
3. `sudo rm -rf /opt/serverpulse-agent /etc/serverpulse`
4. `sudo userdel serverpulse` (if no other services use it)

## Dependencies

- Phases 0-5 complete (backend ingest endpoint, auth by agent token, WS pub/sub)
- Python 3.8+ on target machine
- `psutil` and `requests` packages

## Success Criteria

- [ ] Agent script runs standalone, collects metrics every 15s
- [ ] Metrics arrive at backend ingest endpoint (verified via logs + DB query)
- [ ] Metrics published via WebSocket (verified via wscat)
- [ ] install.sh completes successfully on clean Ubuntu 24.04
- [ ] systemd service starts, restarts on crash, stops cleanly on SIGTERM
- [ ] Retry logic works: simulated backend downtime → backoff → recovery
